course: dictionary
lesson: 3013
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can mean different things in different places. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The African dwarf crocodile is one of the smallest crocodiles, usually under two metres.» Here dwarf describes a much smaller kind of crocodile, so the clue is size.
explain: «The skyscraper dwarfed the houses.» Here dwarfed is a verb. It means the skyscraper made the houses look tiny by being much bigger. Ask yourself whether the word is a thing, a describing word, or an action. The job the word does in the sentence helps you find its meaning.
explain: In a fairy tale, dwarf means something else again: a small, strong creature who lives in mountains and mines. Stories like «Snow White» use it this way. Check the words around it, then put your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Dwarf can be a noun, an adjective or a verb.
fact: As a noun, a dwarf is a small, strong, often bearded creature in fairy tales and fantasy, living in mountains and mines.
fact: As an adjective, dwarf means much smaller than usual, as in «a dwarf tree» or «a dwarf planet».
fact: To dwarf something means to make it look very small by being much bigger, as in «dwarfed by» a tall building.
fact: A «white dwarf» is a small star that is dying. It is about the size of the Earth but so heavy that a teaspoon of it would weigh more than a car.
exercise: «The African dwarf crocodile is one of the smallest crocodiles.» In this sentence, what does dwarf mean? | *A kind of crocodile that is much smaller than usual | To make something look tiny by being bigger | A small, bearded creature who lives in mountains | A type of hornbill bird
exercise: «The skyscraper dwarfed the houses.» What does dwarfed mean here? | Painted the houses bright colours | *Made the houses look tiny by being much bigger | Built the houses out of stone | Gave the houses a bigger garden
exercise: In «Snow White», what is a dwarf? | A tall tree in a forest | A bird that hunts insects in the savanna | *A small, strong, bearded creature who lives in mountains and mines | A dying star
test: What is a dwarf planet? | A planet that is very hot | A planet with a ring of ice around it | *A planet much smaller than the usual planets | A planet that gives out its own light
test: In «the skyscraper dwarfed the houses», what part of speech is dwarfed? | Adverb | Adjective | Noun | *Verb
exam: Which sentence uses dwarf as an adjective? | *The gardener planted a dwarf apple tree | The tower dwarfed the church | The dwarf dug for gold in the mine | The dwarf lived under the mountain
